# Keep this file explicit: every entry is a path the Docker build never reads,
# and a broad glob here silently drops files a later COPY needs.
#
# Because the exclusions are pattern-level (node_modules, dist, *.md), the
# files the Dockerfile copies explicitly must stay visible: web/package.json,
# web/bun.lock, web/.npmrc, relaykit/ and tokenkit/ Go sources, VERSION, and
# the repository-root licence files.

# Repository automation and editor state.
.github
.git
.vscode
.vscode-test
.idea
.devcontainer
.githooks
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.dockerignore

# Documentation and the Electron wrapper (its own npm project).
*.md
docs
electron

# Development-only tooling and local artifacts.
Makefile
makefile
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.dev.yml
typescript
bin
e2e
integration
.reports
.eslintcache
.gocache
.golangci.yml
.tool-versions
*.log
*.sh
.env*

# Frontend trees that are installed or generated inside the image.
/web/node_modules
/web/dist
/web/coverage
/web/.tanstack
/web/.bun
/web/.rsbuild
/web/src/i18n/locales/_reports

# Local Go build output.
/new-api
/new-api-*
*.test
*.exe

# The only negation this file can carry safely: no directory leading to this
# path is excluded, and the pattern that would otherwise drop it is a
# file-name glob rather than a directory rule.
!THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md
